A year earlier, senior knights of the Order had gathered in the stone council 
chamber at Rhodes to elect Philippe de Villiers de LIsle-Adam, then grand 
prior of France and serving the king, Francis I, at Bourgogne, as their new 
grand master. 


It was a respectable choice, L Isle-Adam’s family had provided many knights 


